# Check every text file out with LF, on every platform.
#
# Two committed files here are generated and byte-compared in CI: dist/index.js
# and templates/deploy.yml. Git for Windows converts to CRLF on checkout by
# default, which would make a freshly built file differ from the committed one
# purely by line ending -- a drift failure with nothing actually drifting.
#
# It matters beyond the comparison: templates/deploy.yml carries a shell script
# inside a YAML block scalar, and src/gitlab/deploy.sh is that script. Neither
# should depend on the checkout settings of whoever last built them.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary fixtures, so they are never line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.zip binary
*.tar.gz binary
